**What the intervals support (and nothing else):**

- At **p=0.003**, UF Wilson intervals for **d=7** and **d=3** are disjoint (hi 0.004705 < lo 0.006342). Same-shot binomial CIs therefore separate those two LERs. d=5 vs d=3 at this p still overlap.
- At **p=0.001**, UF is 0/1200 for all three distances; the Wilson upper bound is 0.003191. No ranking is possible.
- At **p=0.005**, UF **point** LER is higher at d=7 than at d=5 (23/1200 vs 14/1200); the Wilson intervals **overlap**. Do not call this anti-threshold.
- No p_th is fitted. Huang’s ~0.62% / ~0.72% figures are a **different** circuit-noise family; they only motivate why this grid sits at 0.1%–0.6%.

